-- title:
--   The far shooting family does not end at rest on the line through the primary
-- statement:
--   Fix $0<\mu<1$ and a Jacobi energy $-c$ below the first critical value. Let $\Sigma_{\mu,c}$ be the selected Levi-Civita component and $\varphi$ a continuous flow on it generated by the Hamiltonian vector field of $K_{\mu,c}$. Write $(x_1,x_2)$ for the physical position relative to the primary $J$ and $(v_1,v_2)$ for the physical (Jacobi) velocity. Let $F(r)$ be the perpendicular far start at $z=(0,r)$.
--
--   **The far family does not end at rest.** Let $b>0$ be a first bad parameter of the far family: $F(r)$ admits a far shooting arc for every $0<r<b$, but $F(b)$ does not. Suppose the forward orbit of $F(b)$ stays in $\{x_1<0,\ x_2<0,\ v_1>0\}$ for $0<t<T$, and at time $T$ reaches the vertical line $x_1=0$ below the axis with $v_1=0$. Then
--   $$v_2\neq0\quad\text{at time } T,$$
--   that is, the orbit does not arrive at rest on the zero-velocity curve exactly on the line through $J$.
--
--   Birkhoff's shooting argument (1915, §18) lets the far family end in a collision or in a vertical tangency ($\tau=\pm\pi/2$); he does not discuss this degenerate case. In the formal reduction of `birkhoff_far_arc_limit` it is the only ingredient not proved: collisions, tangencies, interior zeros of $v_1$ (via Birkhoff's identity (59) and his third-derivative argument), and orbits that never reach the line are all handled. Numerically this degeneration was never observed.
-- source:
--   Birkhoff 1915, The restricted problem of three bodies, §18, pp. 740–742 (Rend. Circ. Mat. Palermo 39)

import Definitions.Def_BirkhoffShootingArcs

namespace BirkhoffGlobalSection

theorem birkhoff_far_no_rest_end (μ c : ℝ)
    (hμ0 : 0 < μ) (hμ1 : μ < 1)
    (hc : belowFirstCriticalValue μ c)
    (φ : Flow ℝ (LeftEnergyState μ c))
    (hφ : IsLeviCivitaHamiltonianFlow μ c φ)
    (b : ℝ) (hb : 0 < b)
    (hgood : ∀ r ∈ Set.Ioo 0 b, ∃ x : LeftEnergyState μ c, (x : Phase) = farShootingStart μ c r ∧ ∃ τ : ℝ, IsFarShootingArc φ x τ)
    (hbad : ¬ (∃ x : LeftEnergyState μ c, (x : Phase) = farShootingStart μ c b ∧ ∃ τ : ℝ, IsFarShootingArc φ x τ))
    (xb : LeftEnergyState μ c) (hxb : (xb : Phase) = farShootingStart μ c b)
    (T : ℝ) (hT : 0 < T)
    (hq : ∀ t ∈ Set.Ioo 0 T,
      relativePosition μ ((φ t xb : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase) 0 < 0 ∧
      relativePosition μ ((φ t xb : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase) 1 < 0 ∧
      0 < jacobiVelocity (leviCivitaToJacobi μ ((φ t xb : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase)) 0)
    (hX : relativePosition μ ((φ T xb : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase) 0 = 0)
    (hY : relativePosition μ ((φ T xb : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase) 1 < 0)
    (hv : jacobiVelocity (leviCivitaToJacobi μ ((φ T xb : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase)) 0 = 0) :
    jacobiVelocity (leviCivitaToJacobi μ ((φ T xb : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase)) 1 ≠ 0 := by sorry

end BirkhoffGlobalSection
